// expect: refuse E_EffectMismatch
// A SUGAR CALLS THE LANGUAGE'S VOCABULARY, never what its name binds where it
// stands: `xs[i]` calls the prelude's list_index and a rest pattern cuts with
// its slice, so each charges that declaration's row whatever the local scope
// binds. Measured on boot 0a0cc116 before the charge resolved its callee at
// the link's own scope: a parameter named `list_index` swallowed the index's
// charge and `with !Memory` was accepted over a body that reads memory, and
// a parameter named `slice` did the same for the rest's `!Alloc` — a false
// proof of each negative. Under a neutral parameter name both refused.
fn first(list_index, xs) with !Memory = xs[0] + list_index

fn after_head(slice, xs) with !Alloc = match xs {
  [_, ...rest] => len(rest) + slice,
  [] => slice,
}

fn main() = first(1, [5, 6]) + after_head(2, [7, 8, 9])
